// D1699 — the `??` DEFAULT's kind decides the result's rep, and the lowering read the left
// operand's residual atom instead. An `i32 | null` operand with a `"x"` default joins to
// `i32 | string` and is a box; with `1.5` it widens to `f64`; with `0` it stays the unboxed
// i32. All three were one blocktype — the operand's — so two of them staged the wrong rep.
//
// The operand is NULL, so every line proves the DEFAULT's own rep survived to the print. The
// last line is the if-expression context, which reaches the join through a second blocktype.
//
// A STRUCT default is not here and has a row (D1703): it is check-clean invalid wasm at both
// faces and would grade every cell of this matrix, so it carries its own witness instead. The
// `argument` un-annotated cell is the monomorphization pin and stays SILENT on both seeds —
// D1702, left graded rather than skipped because it is this template's own un-annotated face.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@SKIP@@
map_value: the builder guards its read with `!= null`, and this template's operand is null by
design so the DEFAULT is what each line proves — the guarded body never runs
// @@PRELUDE@@
function mkN(): i32 | null { return null }
function big(): i64 { return 9 }
// @@VALUE@@
mkN()
// @@TYPE@@
i32 | null
// @@PROOF@@
print(v ?? 0)
print(v ?? "x")
print(v ?? 1.5)
print(v ?? true)
print(v ?? big())
const r = if 1 == 1 { v ?? "j" } else { "y" }
print(r)
// @@WANT@@
0 then x then 1.5 then true then 9 then j
